  "worked_solution": "Suppose $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ where $f(t)$ is a continuous function of exponential order $a$ on $[0,\\infty ).$ If ${f}^{\u2032}(t)$ is continuous and ${f}^{\u2033}(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty ),$ then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{\u2033}(t)} & ={s}^{2}L{f(t)}-sf(0)-{f}^{\u2032}(0).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can calculate the Laplace transform of ${f}^{\u2033}(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{f}^{\u2033}(t)} & ={s}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-{s}^{2}}-s\\cdot (0)-(-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{s}^{2}}{s(1-s)}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{1-s}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{s+1-s}{1-s} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1-s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>1.$",
